				{
					"id": "tVz42XywWNxdrRj8P",
					"name": "Enhanced Dodge",
					"reference": "B51",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Framework.md calls this out by name: superior Aeldari reflexes translate into an Enhanced Dodge for Aspect Warriors specifically, on top of Guardian-tier speed — a Dire Avenger or Howling Banshee weaving through incoming fire in a way no unaugmented human, Guardsman or Guardian, quite manages.\n\nDesign: Enhanced Dodge 1 (B51, 15 points/level).",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Aeldari"
					],
					"points_per_level": 15,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 1
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TUe8O6QlMqT8ztm5Y",
			"name": "Autarch's Mastery",
			"local_notes": "Lore: What an Autarch actually is: not a bigger Exarch and not a Farseer with a sword, but an Aeldari who has walked several Paths far enough to master each without being lost to any of them, and who a craftworld therefore trusts to command a warhost drawn from every Aspect Shrine, Guardian defense force, and allied Path all at once.\n\nDesign: 110 (Attribute Modifiers) + 15 (further Enhanced Dodge) + 15 (Combat Reflexes) + 25 (Weapon Master) + 30 (Trained By A Master) + 5 (Enhanced Parry 1) + 10 (Charisma 2) + 15 (Reputation) + 1 (Master of Many Paths) = 226 points, added to the Aspect Warrior package's 249 for 475 points of physiology and command presence before skills. See the Autarch template, which lands above both the Exarch and Farseer totals per framework.md's own direction that an Autarch sits higher than either.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Aeldari"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tEGRf8Z8xBu51DX3R",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Autarch)",
					"local_notes": "Design: Framework target over the Aspect Warrior + Keen Battle-Sense baseline: ST 12, DX 18, IQ 14, HT 12, Per 15 (free: IQ 14 + Keen Battle-Sense's existing +1), Will 17 (free: IQ 14 + Aspect Training's existing +1 Will + this trait's own +2 Will, below) — set deliberately above every named anchor (Exarch's IQ 13/Will 15, Farseer's DX 14) per framework.md's own direction that an Autarch sits higher than either. Increased ST +1 (B14, 10/level, 10) for ST 12, matching an Exarch's own frame. Increased DX +2 (B15, 20/level, 40) for DX 18, matching an Exarch's own peerless reflexes rather than exceeding them — an Autarch's edge over an Exarch is breadth and command, not a faster blade. Increased IQ +2 (B16, 20/level, 40) for IQ 14: a keener strategic mind than any single-Path specialist, per Codex background's treatment of Autarchs as a craftworld's finest tacticians. Increased HT +1 (B15, 10/level, 10) for HT 12. Increased Will +2 (B16, 5/level, 10) on top of Aspect Training's own +1, for Will 17. 10+40+40+10+10 = 110 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical"
					],
					"base_points": 110,
